209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (What this year made undeniably clear is that belonging and community are not optional. Without connection, even food and shelter fall short. To truly heal and rebuild, people need to be seen. To be known. To be valued.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We leaned into that truth this year. We launched a peer mentorship program for neighbors exiting the sex trade, training mentors with lived experience. We partnered with the University of Washington to pilot on-demand therapy sessions. And each day, we opened our doors to 200+ neighbors seeking not just survival, but dignity and connection.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
