338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In July 2022, we welcomed a 53-year-old neighbor living in a tent after moving here from out of state. She was navigating homelessness, substance use disorder, and the trauma of commercial sexual exploitation. Within a month of building relationship with our community advocate, she moved into a tiny home village.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By February 2024, she was working with a Housing Specialist and Mental Health Practitioner through our partner UW Harborview and was approved for a specialized housing voucher. Our advocate remained a steady presence, supporting her through apartment tours, appointments, and her methadone treatment.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (When she fell behind on rent that fall, our advocate helped her apply for rental assistance. Despite receiving an eviction notice in March 2025, she was allowed to stay while she looked for new housing. In July, she moved into a new apartment, and joined our peer mentor program for survivors of commercial sexual exploitation!)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
